# Zindeks-First Search

Use zindeks first for codebase search and structural questions in this repo.

- Keyword search: use `zindeks search "<query>"` or MCP `search_code(query)`.
- Symbols: use MCP `search_graph(name_pattern)`.
- Callers/callees: use MCP `trace_call_path(name, direction)`.
- Architecture: use MCP `get_architecture()`.
- Read a file: use MCP `read_file(path, offset, limit)` (numbered, paged).
- List files: use MCP `list_files(pattern, dir)` instead of Glob/dir.
- File outline: use MCP `file_outline(path)` for symbols without full content.

Avoid broad shell search (`rg`, `grep`, `git grep`, `findstr`, `Select-String`,
recursive `Get-ChildItem`/`gci`, or `dir /s`) until zindeks has been tried, unless
the file type is generated/binary or outside the zindeks index.

If the MCP server says no project is loaded, call `index_repository` with the
absolute repo path or run `zindeks index .` from the repo root.
